! Floating-point diagnostic jb_af1c, routine F210 "STORE ROUNDED TEST
! ROUTINE", section D "TESTS OF INDICATORS", sub-tests D1-D2
! (docs/jb_af1c_floating-point.pdf p.112, octal 016130.40-016137.40,
! the routine's own exit "BD,$+1.0"). Thirteen rows, and it closes
! F210 out.
!
! D2 is the one this whole routine has been missing. Every block from
! A1 to C2 checked what SRD STORED; none of them ever asked about an
! indicator, and the LOST CARRY indicator in particular has been
! recorded as uncovered since F210A5 -- which produces the very
! overflow that sets it and then never looks.
!
!   D1  BMOPZ clears MOP and branches; DL(U) FPK0; SRD(U) ROS; then
!       BZMOP, "error if MOP indicator off". SRD is a to-memory
!       operation, so it must set MOP.
!   D2  BLCZ clears LC; DL(U) FPK32 with C0011 dropping FPK32's own
!       all-ones fraction into the low half, so the accumulator
!       fraction is 96 ones at exponent +2 -- the same operand F210A5
!       uses. SRD(U) rounds, the +1 at IBM 60 carries the whole way
!       out, and the overflow bit must set LC. Then BZLC, "error if LC
!       indicator off".
!
! So A5 and D2 are the two halves of one rule. A5 asks what the
! overflow did to the STORED WORD (nothing -- the exponent stays +2),
! and D2 asks what it did to the INDICATOR (set it). The model gets
! both from the same lostCarry that fpNormalize96Wide returns when
! unnormalized, and until D2 only half of that was under a run.
!
! FSR3 is the listing's own label at 016111.40, in F210C; this block
! carries no label of its own.
!
! ROS (022355) is the routine's scratch word, not a pool constant.
! Framework substitutes as everywhere else in this series: SERS (octal
! 1304) -> FAIL halt, SEN (octal 1310) -> scratch. Constants from the
! pool p.176. PASS sits at 016137.40, on the routine's exit; the four
! rows after it (BD,$+1.0 / B,FSR3 / SIC,SENO+.32 / B,SSW) are the
! SSIP return and are not transcribed.
!
! Instructions: B, BMOPZ, BZMOP, BLCZ, BZLC, DL(U), C0011, SRD(U), SIC.
! verify_fp_arith_f210d_listing.py checks every word bit-for-bit.
!
! Observed: both passed on the first run, and both questions are live.
! Suppressing MOP halts D1 with SIC storing 016133.40; suppressing LC
! halts D2 with SIC storing 016137.40 -- each the address right after
! its own branch.
!
! The LC result is the one that closes a gap this routine had carried
! from the start. F210A5 stays GREEN under the same suppression, and
! so does F210C. A5 runs the identical operand and produces the
! identical overflow, but asks only what the overflow did to the
! stored word; D2 is the only thing in the suite that asks what it did
! to the indicator. The two are complementary halves of the
! unnormalized-overflow rule, not duplicates of each other.

! -- SSIP framework substitutes --
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- the routine's scratch word --
        SLC, (8)22355.0
ROS     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- constants (pool p.176) --
        SLC, (8)022005.0
FPK0    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000000000000000000000
        SLC, (8)022045.0
FPK32   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001177777777777777760

! The listing prints no label at 016130.40 -- ENTRY is ours, needed
! only as the END operand.
! -- code (verbatim, at the listing's addresses) --
        SLC, (8)16130.40
ENTRY   B, $+.32                               ! F210D1: test MOP indicator, on condition
        BMOPZ, $+.32
        DL(U), FPK0
        SRD(U), ROS
        SIC, SEN
        BZMOP, SERS                            ! error if MOP indicator off
        B, $+.32                               ! F210D2: test LC indicator, on condition
        BLCZ, $+.32
        DL(U), FPK32
        C0011(BU,48), FPK32+.12, 20
        SRD(U), ROS
        SIC, SEN
        BZLC, SERS                             ! error if LC indicator off
PASS    BEW, $                                 ! 016137.40: the routine's exit ("BD,$+1.0")
        END, ENTRY
